From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:20:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 48/94] drm/msm: reset the GPU on a hardware fault with no
 submit to blame

recover_worker() named the guilty submit from the fence memptr (memptr +
1 on the CP's ring) and bailed when that submit was gone. With a memptr
that went backwards (seen on A512 after "CP | opcode error": completed
fence 130748, submitted 130961) every hangcheck queued a recovery that
found nothing, for minutes, and the GPU was never reset. The same
bail-out leaves a GPU that faulted after writing its last fence (or with
a preemption that failed and stays FAULTED) wedged.

Recovery requests now carry a reason: MSM_GPU_RECOVER_HANG from the
hangcheck, MSM_GPU_RECOVER_HW_FAULT through msm_gpu_hw_fault() from
every adreno fault path (hang detect and CP error irqs, preemption
timeouts and failures, GMU faults). The worker blames the oldest submit
on the hung ring whose fence has not signalled (on a ring the CP is not
on only for a hang), and a hardware fault resets the GPU even when no
submit is left to blame. A run queued by a fault reported during a
recovery finds no reason left and does nothing, instead of blaming the
freshly replayed submit.

The hangcheck timer is stopped for the recovery and re-armed a full
period out while work is pending. Fences are updated only after the
reset, so none signals on the hung submit's account while the GPU may
still run it, never backwards, and not from a memptr that was ahead of
the last fence before the reset. This contains the put_task_struct()
of "drm/msm: Fix task_struct reference leak in recover_worker" and the
reset before retire of "drm/msm: Recover HW before retire hung submit",
which this tree did not have. The a5xx preemption timer of a switch the
reset ended is deleted in a5xx_preempt_hw_init().

